course: dictionary
lesson: 1005
title: Bolshevik: a name with a history
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: «Bolshevik» is a name for a group of people. A Bolshevik was a member of a group of Russian communists, led by Lenin. Context helps you here: in «At Kruty a few hundred defenders fought a much larger Bolshevik force», the word force tells you the Bolsheviks were a group of fighters.
explain: The word can also describe things. In «the Bolshevik Revolution», Bolshevik is an adjective: it tells you which revolution it was. It is the revolution the Bolsheviks carried out in Russia, and it began a new kind of government.
explain: Slang can change a word's meaning. «Bolshie» or «bolshy» is old British slang that means stubborn and rebellious, and it comes from this word. Test it: «My sister is being bolshie about her bath.» Swap in stubborn and the sentence still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
fact: A Bolshevik was a member of a group of Russian communists, led by Lenin.
fact: The Bolsheviks took power in Russia in a revolution and later created the Soviet Union.
fact: The name comes from the Russian word «bolshinstvo», which means majority.
fact: Always write Bolshevik with a capital B, because it is the name of a group.
fact: Old British slang «bolshie» or «bolshy» means stubborn and rebellious.
exercise: «At Kruty a few hundred defenders fought a much larger Bolshevik force.» What is a Bolshevik? | A kind of Russian bread | A horse cart with a machine gun | *A member of a group of Russian communists | A student volunteer defending a city
exercise: In «the Bolshevik Revolution», which word tells you which revolution it was? | *Bolshevik | Revolution | the
exercise: Tom says, «My sister is being bolshie about her bath.» What does bolshie mean? | Fast asleep | *Stubborn and rebellious | Happy and singing | Very clean
test: Why does Bolshevik start with a capital letter? | Because it starts a sentence | *Because it is the name of a group | Because it is a very long word | Because it is a question
test: The word Bolshevik comes from the Russian «bolshinstvo», which means what? | Small | *Majority | Revolution | Stubborn
exam: In «Nestor Makhno was finally defeated by the Bolsheviks», what does defeated mean? | Made into a king | *Beaten, lost the fight | Invited to dinner | Given a present
